### Fingerprint Attendance — API examples
### Walkthrough: log in -> create device -> create member -> enrol -> verify (check-in) -> verify (check-out) -> history

@host = http://localhost:5089
@token = PASTE_JWT_FROM_LOGIN_HERE
# Required only if Fingerprint:DeviceApiKey is configured on the server; otherwise ignored.
@deviceApiKey = PASTE_DEVICE_API_KEY_HERE
@deviceId = PASTE_DEVICE_ID_HERE
@memberId = PASTE_MEMBER_ID_HERE
@templateId = PASTE_TEMPLATE_ID_HERE

# NOTE: capturedTemplate is a base64-encoded vendor template (NEVER a raw image).
# For the Mock provider, any base64 string works; the SAME string must be used at
# enrol and verify time to produce a match. The value below is base64("demo-finger-001...").
@template = ZGVtby1maW5nZXItMDAxLTAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwMDA=

### 0. Log in as admin to obtain a JWT (admin can manage devices)
POST {{host}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Matkhau@2"
}

### 1. Create an attendance device (Admin only) -> copy "id" into @deviceId
POST {{host}}/api/AttendanceDevice
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Front Door Scanner",
  "location": "Main entrance",
  "vendor": "Mock",
  "serialNumber": "SN-0001",
  "isActive": true
}

### 2. List devices
GET {{host}}/api/AttendanceDevice?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Create a member -> copy "id" into @memberId
POST {{host}}/api/Member
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "fullName": "Nguyen Van A",
  "phoneNumber": "0987654321",
  "status": 1
}

### 4. Register (enrol) a fingerprint for the member -> copy "id" into @templateId
POST {{host}}/api/Fingerprint
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "memberId": "{{memberId}}",
  "fingerPosition": 1,
  "capturedTemplate": "{{template}}",
  "vendor": "Mock",
  "quality": 90
}

### 5. List the member's registered fingerprints (template bytes are never returned)
GET {{host}}/api/Fingerprint/member/{{memberId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Update a fingerprint (re-enrol the same finger)
PUT {{host}}/api/Fingerprint/{{templateId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "memberId": "{{memberId}}",
  "fingerPosition": 1,
  "capturedTemplate": "{{template}}",
  "vendor": "Mock",
  "quality": 95
}

### 7. Verify a scan -> first scan creates a CHECK-IN (no auth: called by the device)
POST {{host}}/api/Fingerprint/verify
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Api-Key: {{deviceApiKey}}

{
  "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}",
  "capturedTemplate": "{{template}}"
}

### 8. Verify the same scan again -> performs CHECK-OUT (active session is closed)
POST {{host}}/api/Fingerprint/verify
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Api-Key: {{deviceApiKey}}

{
  "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}",
  "capturedTemplate": "{{template}}"
}

### 9. Member attendance history (check-in / check-out sessions, newest first)
GET {{host}}/api/Attendance/member/{{memberId}}?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Delete (soft-delete) a fingerprint
DELETE {{host}}/api/Fingerprint/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Negative: verify with an unknown device -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/Fingerprint/verify
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Api-Key: {{deviceApiKey}}

{
  "deviceId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "capturedTemplate": "{{template}}"
}

### 11b. Negative: verify without the device API key -> 401 (only when DeviceApiKey is configured)
POST {{host}}/api/Fingerprint/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}",
  "capturedTemplate": "{{template}}"
}

### 12. Negative: enrol without a token -> 401 Unauthorized
POST {{host}}/api/Fingerprint
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "memberId": "{{memberId}}",
  "fingerPosition": 0,
  "capturedTemplate": "{{template}}",
  "vendor": "Mock"
}
